---
id: floor
course: test
title: Who may speak
cover: optional
source: A short test of raised hands, open mics and staff. Not a lesson.
---
title: Who may speak
say: This class starts with hands. Raise a hand if you want to speak.
say: Here is some talking to fill the time, one sentence after another.
say: And another sentence, so that there is something to wait behind.
say: The lecturer keeps going until it gives someone the floor.
say: Here is one more sentence of the lesson.
say: And one more after that.
say: Here is a poll. It is in the chat.
poll: Which do you find easier? | Working on paper | Working in your head | About the same
say: Give a thumbs up if you can hear this.
say: Now a short task. Press done when you have finished it.
pause: 30 Press done when you have finished.
poll: close
say: Now the mics are open for a discussion. Unmute if you want to say something.
mic: open What do you think so far?
pause: 9 Unmute and say what you think.
say: Thank you. Hands again now.
mic: hands
say: This sentence is here for the helper to talk over.
say: And this one is here in case the helper needs a bit longer.
say: The helper may also share a screen at any time.
say: That is the end of the test.
